= Campaign Funds

Elections are expensive and our resources are running low... 

Neither of these options are ideal.

- @emergency_campaign: Let us ask our members for (a lot of) assistance.
- @unions_beg: Call up the LO leadership...
- @dkf_beg: Knock on the doors of DKF...
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@emergency_campaign
subtitle: +2 resources – This will cause dissent.
on-arrival: resources += 2; memberrise -= 0.6/efc; homeowner_a -= 2/efc; public_homeowner_a -= 2/efc; rural_a -= 2/efc; pettyb_a -= 2/efc; right_worker_dissent += 6; left_worker_dissent += 4; technocrat_dissent += 3; left_dissent += 5

We run an intensive fundraising campaign inside our party, unfortunately the conservative press takes notice. 'If the socialdemocrats can't even plan their own economy, how do they think they...' we can only hope they laugh themselves to death.


@unions_beg
subtitle: +2 resources – This will worsen our relations with LO.
on-arrival: resources += 2; lo_relations -= 7

LO is not amused, but they dont refuse either. Funds are added, they advice us to be more cautious with our finances in the future.

@dkf_beg
subtitle: +1 resources – This will worsen our relations with DKF.
on-arrival: resources += 1; DKF_relations -= 7; cooperativehealth -= 0.05

Given their already dire economic situation, the cooperatives are somewhat reluctant to assist us. They emphasize that such last minute measures, should be avoided going forwards.